        "text": "The http probe is huge and doesn't test my new `/injections` endpoint (it's not in the list). It's a comprehensive probe that will just run past my endpoint. My endpoint must not break anything. Since it uses `AGENT_TOKEN: \"\"` (no auth token → auth middleware allows all? let me check — `createAuthMiddleware(process.env.AGENT_TOKEN?.trim() || null, ...)` with null token → probably allows all requests). So my endpoint will be reachable if hit, but the probe doesn't hit it.\n\nImportant: the http probe restarts the server many times with different env. My new module `injection.ts` is imported by lifecycle.ts and index.ts at module load. I must ensure it doesn't crash at import time (no side effects that read env unexpectedly or throw). It's a pure module. Good.\n\nAlso, the audit switch `AGENT_INJECTION_AUDIT` default true — I'll read env at request time (not module load), to be safe. Actually `injectionAuditEnabled()` reads `process.env` when called. Fine.\n\nNow let me also double-check: does adding an import of `./agent/injection.ts` in `index.ts` and `lifecycle.ts` cause any circular dependency issues? `injection.ts` will import `INJECTION_GUARD` and `injectionGuardEnabled` from `./injection-guard.ts` (in same `agent/` dir). injection-guard.ts has no imports. So injection.ts → injection-guard.ts (no cycle). lifecycle.ts → injection.ts. index.ts → injection.ts. No cycles. Good.\n\nWait — but `index.ts` imports from `./agent.ts` which imports lifecycle etc. Let me check that `agent.ts` is the aggregator. Actually index.ts imports `startChatCompaction` from `./agent.ts`. Let me check `agent.ts` exists and re-exports. Let me verify.\n\nActually the imports in index.ts line 19-52 are from `\"./agent.ts\"`. And session.ts is `./agent/session.ts`. So `agent.ts` is likely a re-export barrel. Let me check it to understand where to add the audit function import. Let me read agent.ts.\n\nAlso I need to decide: should the audit logic live in `injection.ts` and be imported directly into index.ts, or re-exported via agent.ts? index.ts already imports lots from `./agent.ts`. I'll import the injection audit helper directly from `./agent/injection.ts` in index.ts (consistent with line 149 which imports `markRecoverResume, recoverNoteEnabled` from `./agent/recover-note.ts` directly). So direct import is fine.\n\nLet me check agent.ts to be thorough about startChatCompaction re-export (I'm editing session.ts, which is imported by agent.ts). Let me read agent.ts."
