      "reasoning": "Now I need to verify `input.conversationId` typechecks against `InjectionContext.conversationId: number | string`. `ConversationId` is `number & {brand}` → assignable to `number`. So `{ conversationId: input.conversationId }` → `{ conversationId: ConversationId }` assignable to `InjectionContext`? The property type `ConversationId` is assignable to `number | string`. Yes.\n\nNow add the audit endpoint in index.ts. Let me add the import and the endpoint. I'll add the import near the other agent imports and the endpoint near the other `/chat/:conversationId/*` GET endpoints (e.g., after the context endpoint or near messages). Let me add it after the `/context` endpoint block, or better, as a standalone near the compact/context area. Actually, let me place it right after the `messages` endpoint (line 1029) since it's a GET on the same path prefix. Actually, let me place it near the other GET audit-like endpoints. I'll add it after the `context` endpoint block ends. But I need to find a clean insertion point. Let me add it right after the `/messages` endpoint (after line 1029) — that's a natural place.\n\nActually, to keep it simple and avoid disturbing numbered sections, I'll insert the endpoint right after line 1029 (end of `/messages` GET). Let me re-read that area to get exact text.\n\nActually, I'll add it after the `/context` endpoint's closing (need to find where that block ends). Let me look at lines 1262-1320 to find the end of the context endpoint. Actually simpler: I'll insert right after the `/messages` handler (line 1029 `});`). Let me use a unique anchor: the `handoffMemoryOf` function declaration follows the messages endpoint. I'll insert between them.\n\nLet me first add the import in index.ts.\n\nThe import should be: `import { auditInjections, injectionAuditEnabled } from \"./agent/injection.ts\";`\n\nWhere to add? Near line 149 which imports from `./agent/recover-note.ts`. Let me add it there. Let me look at that area again:\n\n```\n// 恢复注记（2026-11-09 任务书 T3 §5）：只有进程内记账，无存储依赖。\nimport { markRecoverResume, recoverNoteEnabled } from \"./agent/recover-note.ts\";\n```\n\nI'll add after it.\n\nThen add the endpoint. Let me design the endpoint:\n\n```ts\n/**\n * 注入审计（2026-11-10 批 26b §二 / #7 批 A）。\n *\n * `GET /api/v1/agent/chat/:conversationId/injections` → `[{id, source, scope, length}]`：\n * 框架当前接管的注入清单，**只回元数据、不回正文**（length 是正文字符数）。\n * 开关 `AGENT_INJECTION_AUDIT`（默认开；false → 404，一行回滚）。\n *\n * `conversationId` 只作上下文传入（批 A 的注入是框架级静态 inventory，不按会话变化），\n * 因此不解析 durable 会话、不依赖 LLM 配置、不校验会话存在——这是诊断端点，不是会话数据。\n */\napp.get(\"/api/v1/agent/chat/:conversationId/injections\", (c) => {\n  if (!injectionAuditEnabled()) return c.json({ error: \"not_found\" }, 404);\n  return c.json(auditInjections({ conversationId: c.req.param(\"conversationId\") }));\n});\n```\n\nWait — \"不按会话变化\" — the guard IS injected for all conversations as a section. So audit returning the same list for any conversationId is accurate. Good.\n\nHmm, but does returning 404 when audit switch is off align with \"鉴权失败一律 403 空体\"? No, that's auth. 404 for disabled feature is the repo convention. Fine.\n\nLet me also double check: `c.req.param(\"conversationId\")` returns `string`. Good for InjectionContext.\n\nNow let me add imports and endpoint.\n\nActually, one concern: the hard constraint \"对外 id 一律 uuid\" — the audit endpoint takes a conversationId path param but doesn't echo it or expose internal ids. It returns only `{id, source, scope, length}` where `id` is the injection id (\"injection_guard\"), not a conversation id. So no PII/id leak. Good.\n\nLet me add the import.",
