      "reasoning": "Now run the http probe. But before that, let me also verify the \"逐字节一致\" more rigorously. Actually, I realize I should double-check that removing `INJECTION_GUARD`/`injectionGuardEnabled` from the lifecycle import doesn't leave any unused references that would break typecheck (typecheck passed, so fine). Also I should verify the section still renders correctly. Let me think about whether there's a way the rendered content could differ:\n\nBefore: `render: () => (injectionGuardEnabled() ? INJECTION_GUARD : undefined)` — returns string INJECTION_GUARD (when on) or undefined (off).\nAfter: `render: (input) => collectInjections([guardProvider], { conversationId: input.conversationId }).system[0]?.text`\n- guardProvider (on) returns `{id, text: INJECTION_GUARD, order:0, scope:\"session\", channel:\"system\"}`.\n- collectInjections → all=[entry], sort → [entry], dedup → [entry], system=[entry].\n- `.system[0]?.text` = INJECTION_GUARD. ✓ (same string)\n- guardProvider (off) returns undefined → all=[] → system=[] → `.system[0]?.text` = undefined. ✓ (same undefined)\n\nSo byte-identical. And the section key \"injection_guard\" unchanged, position unchanged (still 4th in the array, after persona/verification_iron_law/clarify_contract). ✓.\n\nGood. Now let me run the http probe. It's a long-running command (~a minute+). Let me run with a longer timeout. Actually the default 120s might be too short; the probe does many restarts with sleeps (0.8s each × ~15 restarts = 12s) plus the reminder sleeps etc. Earlier the full suite... let me estimate. Let me set timeout to 300000 (5 min).\n\nActually, let me run it. I'll capture the tail and also grep for failures. Let me run and check the output carefully — particularly the §4.5 checks and any ✗.\n\nLet me run `pnpm --filter @lifediary/server http`.",
