        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Now I edited http-probe.ts (a TS file) after the §二 typecheck+test. I should re-run typecheck to confirm the probe edit typechecks. Let me run typecheck once more (final). Also let me verify git status — no commit, and the task book file modification that was pre-existing (the design doc was already modified when I started — `git status` showed `docs/设计方案/...md` as modified). Let me check that. Actually, when I started, git status showed the design doc as modified (pre-existing change, not mine). I should leave it as-is (not my change). Let me verify I didn't accidentally touch it. I only read it. Good.\n\nLet me do a final typecheck (covers http-probe.ts edit) and a final test run to be thorough — actually test already passed with the same TS code (http-probe.ts is a script, not part of `src` tests, but it IS part of typecheck). Let me run typecheck once more. Actually, the http probe ran via tsx successfully, which means the TS is at least syntactically valid and type-transpilable. But `tsc --noEmit` is stricter. Let me run it.\n\nAlso, let me double check: did I add `src/agent/injection.test.ts` to package.json test correctly? Yes. And the full test passed with 699 (690+9). Good.\n\nLet me also verify there are no leftover direct `INJECTION_GUARD` references in lifecycle that I might have missed (typecheck would catch unused imports as error if noUnusedLocals is on, but let me check tsconfig). Actually typecheck passed, so it's fine. But let me grep to be sure the import is clean.\n\nLet me run final typecheck + a quick grep sanity check."
